+
+``--secondary-sub-style-override=<yes|no>`` (LYINA extension)
+    Enable independent secondary subtitle style options (default: no).
+    Without this opt-in, secondary subtitles retain the normal primary style
+    inheritance. The display role, not the selected source track ID, owns style.
 
+``--secondary-sub-scale=<0-100>`` (LYINA extension)
+    Scale the secondary subtitle role independently (default: 1). Used only
+    when ``secondary-sub-style-override`` is enabled, including bitmap scaling.
+
+``--secondary-sub-<style-option>`` (LYINA extension)
+    Independent counterparts of the ``sub-`` style options: font, font-size,
+    color, outline-size, outline-color, back-color, shadow-offset, border-style,
+    bold, italic, blur, spacing, margins, alignment, justify, font-provider and
+    fonts-dir. Defaults match the primary style defaults. Existing per-role
+    ASS override policy still controls which embedded ASS styles are replaced.
+    These options do not change subtitle source selection, delay or position.
+
 ``--sub-scale=<0-100>``
     Factor for the text subtitle font size (default: 1).
 
